From 0a5cf2d32b725acbfe8a6e95a8a89b639c3e73d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Grahmann <lars.grahmann@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:53:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/22] synaptics_tudor: Follow the vendor open and enroll
 sequence exactly

A template enrolled in one session did not match in a later one. Open
now does the whole vendor sequence (version, iota, startinfo, af twice
before pairing and once after, frame state, database read), and enroll
commits the same 17 byte payload and asks the database before the end.
Adds tudor-test --keep, tudor-delete and tudor-match (not for upstream).
---
 PROTOCOL.md                               |   3 +
 examples/meson.build                      |   2 +-
 examples/tudor-delete.c                   |  74 +++++++++++
 examples/tudor-match.c                    |  48 +++++++
 examples/tudor-test.c                     |  13 +-
 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor.c | 146 +++++++++++++++++-----
 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor.h |   4 +
 7 files changed, 256 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 examples/tudor-delete.c
 create mode 100644 examples/tudor-match.c

diff --git a/PROTOCOL.md b/PROTOCOL.md
index 0bece407..373ea2db 100644
--- a/PROTOCOL.md
+++ b/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -288,6 +288,9 @@ The driver makes a new random guid per print so each print is a user of
 its own, and puts the libfprint user id string in the payload (cut at 64
 bytes, whether the sensor takes other sizes than 17 is untested).
 
+The Windows driver also asks DB info between commit and end, the driver
+now does too. The payload is 17 bytes like Windows (guid and finger).
+
 DB info after an enroll: users, templates and payloads all go up by one.
 
 ### Identify (opcode 0x99)
